  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that $x=0.5$ radians, what is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
  "worked_solution": "Note the argument of the cosine is given in radians. Using a calculator in \"radians\" mode, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.5)=0.877\\,582…≈0.878\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
